      "quote_or_summary": "After the messenger departs, Feridn calls Irij before him and tells him that his two brothers, older than he is, have allied and threaten to bring a large army against him to seize his kingdom and kill him, and that they will also wage war on Feridn if he supports Irij. When Irij asks what he should do, Feridn replies that Irij is unable to resist even one brother, let alone both, and explains that Feridn himself is aged and wishes to pass his remaining days in retirement and repose. He advises Irij that it is better to pursue peace and friendship and to throw away all desire for dominion, warning him that if the sword of anger is unsheathed and war begins, his head will soon be freed from the cares of government and life.",
      "source_text_path": "texts/public-domain/persian/project-gutenberg/persian-literature-volume-1.md",
