    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Rustem says reconciliation cannot happen because Isfendiyr has reviled Zal and heaped indignities on Rustem, so the contest is unavoidable.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "In the morning Zal weeps bitterly and personally ties on Rustem's armor.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Zal tells Rustem that killing Isfendiyr would render Rustem infamous, and that Rustem's death would leave Sistan prostrate and extinguished.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Zal says his heart shudders at the thought of the battle but believes there is no remedy.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Rustem urges Zal to put his trust in God and not be sorrowful, claiming that when he grasps his sword the enemy's head is lost.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "Rustem declares that his desire is to take Isfendiyr alive and serve him, not to sever his head from his body.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Zal is pleased with Rustem's determination and rejoices at the promise of a happy issue to the engagement.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Rustem arrays himself in war-attire, helmet and breast-plate, and mounts Rakush, who is also armed in barding.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Rustem's troops assemble.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Zal appoints Zura to take charge of the troops and to be careful of his brother when assistance might be necessary.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Zal prostrates himself in prayer, asking God to turn away affliction and grant a prosperous day.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Rustem directs Zura to wait with the troops at a distance while he goes alone to meet Isfendiyr.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Bashtan, seeing Rustem coming alone, thinks he is offering peace and suggests that it is better Rustem should go to Isfendiyr's father of his own accord than in bonds.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Isfendiyr replies that Rustem is coming completely equipped in mail and orders his own arms to be brought.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "Bashtan accuses Isfendiyr of having a wild brain and an impetuous spirit resolved on fighting.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "Rustem ascends a high place and summons Isfendiyr to single combat.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "Isfendiyr tells his brother to stay at a distance with the army and not to interfere unless aid is positively required.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Isfendiyr mounts his night-black charger and hastens toward Rustem.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:21",
      "text": "Rustem proposes that they should wait while the two armies are put in motion against each other, noting that his men of Zabul are few and Isfendiyr has a numerous host.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:22",
      "text": "Isfendiyr rejects Rustem's proposal, pointing out Rustem's lofty position and his own place in a spreading vale, and says he will not give his valiant legions to destruction.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:23",
      "text": "Isfendiyr declares that he needs no aid in battle except God.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:24",
      "text": "Rustem states that he likewise requires no human refuge, only Heaven.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:25",
      "text": "Rustem and Isfendiyr begin their battle by throwing numerous javelins that bruise helms and mail, then fight with shining swords until the swords snap.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:26",
      "text": "They next wield battle-axes, striking powerful blows and each trying to hurl the other from his horse.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:27",
      "text": "Their horses become panting from excessive toil, covered with foam and blood, and the strong armor of steed and rider is torn.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:28",
      "text": "The combatants eventually pause, standing apart to breathe, and are described as being in mutual consternation.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:29",
      "text": "Zura becomes impatient at the delay and advances toward the Iranians.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:30",
      "text": "Zura reproaches the Iranians severely for their cowardice.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:31",
      "text": "Nushwer, the younger son of Isfendiyr, feels ashamed and challenges the bravest of the enemy to fight.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:32",
      "text": "Alwa, one of Rustem's followers, comes forward to meet Nushwer but is defeated and killed.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:33",
      "text": "Zura gallops to the charge in anger, lifts his iron mace, and strikes Nushwer on the head, driving him from his steed as a lifeless corpse.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:34",
      "text": "Seeing their gallant leader Nushwer overthrown, the troops flee in terror.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:35",
      "text": "Thousands are slain during the flight, including Mehrnus, another kinsman of Isfendiyr.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    }
